Wed Aug  5 14:46:48 CEST 2026 - petr.pavlu@suse.com

- rpm/modversions: Allow unpacking consolidated data created by ksymtypes
  `scripts/sequence-patch --kabi` currently uses rpm/modversions to unpack
  consolidated symtypes data. This doesn't work in SL-16.1 where the data is
  created by ksymtypes (from suse-kabi-tools).
  The problem is that when ksymtypes packs individual symtypes files into
  a consolidated file, it uses the original '<path>/<basename>.symtypes'
  filename in file separators. However, rpm/modversions expects the format to
  use '<path>/<basename>.o' instead.
  Update rpm/modversions to recognize the '.symtypes' suffix as well.
