Fri Oct 17 07:59:44 CEST 2025 - tzimmermann@suse.com

- config/x86_64: Enable efidrm and vesadrm in kernel config (bsc#1240624)
  Use efidrm for system framebuffers on EFI systems. Do the same with
  vesadrm on BIOS systems. Disable simpledrm in these cases. The new
  drivers provide better hardware support and features, such as 8-bit
  palette modes and EDID data. Keep simpledrm to handle DT entries of
  type 'simple-framebuffer'.
  (cherry picked from commit ee7f030e08ecd757d8bfaaa083a1dbd2b7130bcd)
- config/riscv64: Enable efidrm in kernel config (bsc#1240624)
  Use efidrm for system framebuffers on EFI systems. Disable simpledrm in
  this case. The new drivers provide better hardware support and features.
  Keep simpledrm to handle DT entries of typy 'simple-framebuffer'.
  (cherry picked from commit af74cb32df6487a73210a3d7f0c8c1c9c6cbab46)
